It is my lunch break.
I am in a phone shop.
I have a phone from Mexico.
The clerk is a young man.
"Do you have a Danish SIM card?" I ask.
"Yes, of course," he answers.
I give him my phone.
He puts the SIM card in the phone.
The phone is ready now.
"Your new number is twelve, thirty-four, fifty-six, seventy-eight," he says.
I have a notebook in my bag.
I write the number.
"Twelve, thirty-four, fifty-six, seventy-eight," I repeat.
"Yes, exactly," says the clerk.
"Thank you for the help," I say.
I have a Danish number now!
I put the phone in my pocket.
